  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5704.03 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5704.03 Definitions. For the purposes of this part, the following terms shall be defined as follows:\n\n(a) “School transportation provider” means a school bus driver or monitor employed by a school bus transportation agency contracting with a public school administrative unit, school district, chartered public school, or public academy, to provide transportation services for children;\n\n(b) “School” means a public school administrative unit, school district, chartered public school, or public academy that has been approved by the New Hampshire state board of education; and\n\n(c) “School bus transportation agency” means a private school bus company contracting with a public school to provide drivers and monitors for the transport and supervision of school children.\n\nSource. #12606, eff 8-17-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5700.html"
}
